@startuml owner-view-gate-protocol
' ============================================================================
' One operation of each kind of the view-gate model: a checkpoint, from the
' owner's current root or from another base; a view-local reset; a spawn;
' close and reopen. Model of leaf G01 of task 7931, revised at commit
' 7851c684e for ruling Q1 option A. Every action is an action of ViewSpec in
' formal/tlaplus/stack_safe_pda/RSpaceJournalPublicationOwner.tla, whose
' configuration is RSpaceJournalPublicationOwnerViews.cfg.
'   BLUE   #BBDEFB  a checkpoint caller's locks: the view gate first, the
'                   owner mutex second
'   AMBER  #FFE0B2  a publication that is still pending: reconciliation and
'                   the outcomes that leave the record open
'   PURPLE #E1BEE7  the decisions of the operation
'   RED    #FFCDD2  the two refusals, before anything is captured
'   GREEN  #C8E6C9  the effects of an admitted checkpoint: completion without
'                   a publication, capture, publish, acknowledge
'   GREY   #CFD8DC  the return, which releases the call's locks
'   YELLOW #FFF9C4  the view-local steps, reset and spawn: no gate or mutex is
'                   taken, and the owner's state is unchanged
'   TEAL   #B2DFDB  close and reopen, only while the owner is quiescent
' Each note has a lighter shade of the colour of the step it explains.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #E1BEE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #455A64

title <b>One operation of each kind in the view-gate model</b>\nA checkpoint takes its gate first and the owner mutex second, and the owner checks before it captures;\na reset and a spawn change only the views; close and reopen need a quiescent owner

start
partition "a checkpoint's locks" {
  :CallCheckpoint(view, permit): the idle caller takes the
  free gate of its permit, its own view's gate in a correct
  call, before it calls the owner.;<<#BBDEFB>>
  :TakeMutex(view): the view now holds the owner mutex.
  Holding it, the owner never waits for a gate (LockOrder).;<<#BBDEFB>>
}
partition "reconcile first" {
  while (a publication is pending?) is (yes)
    :ReconcileFirst(view): the holder can only resolve the record,
    even one captured through the other view's gate.;<<#FFE0B2>>
    note right #FFF3E0
      <b>Resolve</b> compares the owner's root with the record's predecessor.
      RecoveryRequired, root still the predecessor: the predecessor
      stands, the record's gate is freed and the record is cleared.
      RecoveryRequired, root moved: the record enters AwaitingAck.
      AwaitingAck: unless the record was acknowledged once, the base
      of the record's view becomes the root; the gate is freed and
      the record is cleared.
      With the mutex free, ReconcilePending applies the same Resolve.
    end note
  endwhile (no)
}
partition "CheckRequest(view), with no base check" {
  if (the permit is another view's gate?) then (yes)
    :result "refused-permit";<<#FFCDD2>>
  else (no)
    if (the attachment's incarnation differs from the owner's?) then (yes)
      :result "refused-incarnation";<<#FFCDD2>>
    else (no)
      if (is the target <latex>\mathit{Succ}(\mathit{base}, \mathit{view})</latex> the owner's root?) then (yes, only from another base)
        :complete without a publication: no record,
        the root stays, the view's base becomes
        the target, result "acknowledged";<<#C8E6C9>>
      else (no)
        :capture: the pending record takes the view, the permit,
        the base, the owner's root as the predecessor and the
        target, in phase Captured, and the permit's gate is
        marked pending, so the return does not free it.;<<#C8E6C9>>
        note right #E8F5E9
          <b>The two kinds of checkpoint</b>
          From the current base, <latex>\mathit{base} = \mathit{owner.root}</latex>:
          Succ has no fixed point, so the target is never
          the root, and the checkpoint always captures,
          with its base equal to the predecessor.
          From another base, <latex>\mathit{base} \neq \mathit{owner.root}</latex>:
          it captures when the target is not the root,
          with a base that differs from the predecessor,
          and a publication sets the root to the successor
          of a base that was not the root (the witness
          NeverPublishedAcrossBases reaches this case).
        end note
        switch (PublishView(view, outcome): the outcome of the publication?)
        case ()
          :<b>unknown-new</b>: the root and lastPublished
          become the target, the record enters
          RecoveryRequired, the gate stays
          pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
        case ()
          :<b>new</b>: the root and lastPublished become
          the target, and the record enters
          AwaitingAck.;<<#C8E6C9>>
          :AcknowledgeView(view, completes):
          the view's base becomes the new root.;<<#C8E6C9>>
          if (the acknowledgement completes?) then (yes)
            :the gate is freed, the record is
            cleared, result "acknowledged";<<#C8E6C9>>
          else (no)
            :the record keeps one acknowledgement,
            the gate stays pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
          endif
        case ()
          :<b>unknown-old</b>: the root and lastPublished
          stay, the record enters
          RecoveryRequired, the gate stays
          pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
        endswitch
      endif
    endif
  endif
}
:ReturnCall(view): the mutex and every gate that this call holds are freed.
A gate marked pending stays held by its record.;<<#CFD8DC>>
stop

start
partition "view-local steps: no gate or mutex is taken, and the owner's state is unchanged" {
  if (which step?) then (a reset)
    :ResetView(view, target), when the view's caller is idle
    and its own gate is free: the view's base becomes the
    target, and nothing else changes. The owner's root stays
    equal to lastPublished (OwnerRootIsLastPublication).;<<#FFF9C4>>
    note left #FFFDE7
      A checkpoint of the view from this base
      targets <latex>\mathit{Succ}(\mathit{base}, \mathit{view})</latex>; when the
      base is not the owner's root, it is a
      checkpoint from another base.
    end note
  else (a spawn)
    :CallSpawn(view), when both callers are idle and both
    gates are free: the other view's attachment becomes a
    copy of this view's incarnation, base and session
    (SpawnSharesOwner), and this caller's result is "spawned".;<<#FFF9C4>>
    note right #FFFDE7
      A spawn reads nothing of the owner: a view
      spawned from a stale attachment carries
      the stale incarnation, and a checkpoint
      through its own gate is refused with
      "refused-incarnation".
    end note
  endif
}
stop

start
partition "close and reopen" {
  :CloseOwner, only on a live, quiescent owner below its session bound:
  live becomes false and the incarnation advances by one, so every
  attachment taken before the close fails the incarnation check.;<<#B2DFDB>>
  :ReopenOwner(view, incarnation), only on a closed, quiescent owner:
  live becomes true, the incarnation advances by one again
  (FreshIncarnation), the session advances, and the view attaches
  at the owner's root with the new incarnation and session.;<<#B2DFDB>>
  note right #E0F2F1
    A view that kept its old attachment is
    refused with "refused-incarnation".
  end note
}
stop

legend right
  <b>Legend</b>
  <back:#BBDEFB> blue </back> a checkpoint caller's locks
  <back:#FFE0B2> amber </back> a publication still pending
  <back:#E1BEE7> purple </back> a decision of the operation
  <back:#FFCDD2> red </back> a refusal before any capture
  <back:#C8E6C9> green </back> the effects of an admitted checkpoint
  <back:#CFD8DC> grey </back> the return
  <back:#FFF9C4> yellow </back> a view-local step: reset or spawn
  <back:#B2DFDB> teal </back> close and reopen
endlegend
@enduml
